From d8d0dc2d9f09a37504d18eaeee791422bb574760 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FunnyAWM <1142978300@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:19:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(t11): parse real Chromium NetLogs and close Electron
 gracefully

Chromium encodes event types as ids plus a name->id table, so the old
string-prefix filter parsed a real desktop capture to zero hosts: a
networked app looked clean. Resolve ids through constants.logEventTypes,
treat a missing/empty log as a capture failure, and shut the app down
through WM_CLOSE so the JSON is complete instead of truncated.
